WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:03.240
Thank you.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:09.050
We offer you exceptional promotions

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:09.690
Rose

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:49.820
I have money from the lottery!

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:52.280
Wilson!

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.760
Are you there?

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.980
Listen Wilson, I warn you, I don't want to stay in-

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.840
Wilson!

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:03.280
You!

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:09.640
Who's there?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.330
Wilson, it's me, Rose!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.520
Is anyone there?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.020
Wilson?

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.170
Which sound?

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:20.930
Oh, the f**k!

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:00.980
That was funny, you got me.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:06.220
Stop it, I'm done laughing!

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.320
Who came up with this stupid idea?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:09.820
Dédérec!

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:10.790
It's you!

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.260
What is it with you?

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:14.780
No!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:29.160
No!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:29.220
No!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:39.530
away.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.160
I ripped my arm off.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:11.860
Yeah, plastic.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:14.910
Thank you, I noticed.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:18.380
Who was it? Students? There are only students to make jokes.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.360
Why would it be students?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.360
I don't know.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.080
Yet you said it, why students?

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.760
Because to be so many to dress up and dress up, it's probably students.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.090
That's a good reasoning, well done.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:29.960
Thank you.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.940
But you're wrong.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.460
It doesn't matter. When Wilson sees them, he'll call the police.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.080
Who is Wilson?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.120
The chief electrician.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:36.380
They killed him.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.290
It's no fun at all! You're going to stop!

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.390
Stay away! Watch your eyes!

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.170
I've had enough of this stupid joke!

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:47.050
Who are you? And the others down there, who are they?

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.480
I said, who are the little bambas?

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.700
They are in plastic.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.200
Living plastic creatures.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.230
They want to take control of the electric relay on the roof.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.910
It could have been a problem, but fortunately I have that.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.980
So, I'm going to get on the roof.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.430
roof and make them jump. It could be that I die in the explosion but do not worry

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.150
not for me. You, you will go home and prepare a beef bourguignon. If you

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:14.320
talk to someone about what you have seen, his life will be in danger. I am the

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.860
doctor and you call yourself how Rose? It was a pleasure Rose. Run to live!

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.740
The centre of London has been closed due to security reasons for the origin of the explosion.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.140
According to witnesses...

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.700
I know, they talk about it on TV, on all the channels!

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.880
She was lucky, she could have died!

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.460
Seriously, she is so shocked that she took a breath of fresh air!

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.000
Come here, you'll see, it looks like it's me, her daughter!

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:29.820
Oh, look!

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:34.140
I called you on your phone, you could have died, everyone is talking about that.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.260
I can't believe your store exploded.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.840
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:39.610
What happened?

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:40.690
I don't know.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.310
Do you know why it exploded?

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.070
I wasn't even inside, I was in the street when it happened.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:48.170
I'm with Debbie on the phone, she's friends with a Mirror journalist.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.670
He pays 500 pounds for an interview.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:50.910
Oh, that's a good idea, pass me the phone.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.400
You're going to have to make a living now that you don't have any more work,

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.240
and don't count on me to take care of you.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.710
Betty? She's alive! I told her!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.870
Yes, of course she couldn't give an interview, she passed out!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.290
What? You're drinking tea?

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.490
No, no, no, no, it's not good, it's not good. You were shocked, you need something else.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:11.990
But I'm fine.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.670
No, I don't think so, no. We're going to drink something more consistent.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:15.870
We're going to the pub, both of us.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:16.990
There's a match, right?

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.320
No, no, no, I'm just worried about you.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.220
There's a match, I'm sure of it.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.060
That's not the point, but if we hurry, we could see the last five minutes.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.480
Go on alone, I'm going to stay here.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:28.440
Come on, throw that in the trash.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:34.090
Hahahaha

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:37.460
Goodbye!

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:39.710
Bye!

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:45.310
... under the 15 garnisons of firefighters are mobilized.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:48.570
They do everything they can to save the island's infrastructure.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:56.980
All the time!

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:29.660
Yaffin' cheese?

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.430
Try to work there. They're always looking for people.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:34.550
Oh yes, they're monsters.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:36.010
It's better than nothing, isn't it?

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.010
It's in this shop that you've learned everything you know.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:39.610
Don't forget to claim compensation.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:42.420
I'm serious, you were shocked and traumatized.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:47.440
Ariana managed to get 2,000 pounds simply because a client told her she looked like a Greek.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:51.880
It's true that she's Greek, but what's important is that she got Gankos.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.950
Mom, the cash register, it's open. I told you it was...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.420
Leave it closed, all the stray cats will come!

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:02.540
I didn't even touch it!

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:03.970
You only had to think about it!

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:22.580
What are you doing here?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:23.640
This is where I live!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:24.760
You don't have anything better to do?

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:25.890
What are you talking about?

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.390
I'm at home because my job was skipped.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:29.570
That's a good sign.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.550
Are you in plastic? No, skull box.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.110
Well, I'm going.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.560
You, inside, I have two months to tell you.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:35.840
Who's there?

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.050
It's about last night, it's for the investigation.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.290
Leave us ten minutes.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.260
For me, she deserves compensation.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.480
Oh, we're talking about several million.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.440
I'm in a bedroom dress.

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:51.340
Yes, I see.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:55.320
All alone in my room with an unknown.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.000
Yes, that's true.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:11:59.790
Yes.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.620
And everything can happen?

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:03.440
No.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:08.810
Don't be so careless.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.110
Do you want a coffee?

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.480
I'd like some milk.

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.030
We should go see the police.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.120
I'm serious.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:16.050
And together.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:17.790
A homosexual meets an alien.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:18.850
I don't want any of that, you know.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.580
I had the impression that I was made a bad joke.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:22.400
The end is sad.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.620
They said on TV that they had found a body.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:26.360
Rose Tyler.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.590
Oh, it could have been worse.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.240
I thought I was having a bad dream.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.600
I thought it was a joke.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.090
Anyway, before I go see the police,

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.090
I want to know what I'm supposed to tell them.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.150
I want you to tell me the whole story.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.140
What's that?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.040
Do you have a cat?

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:46.850
No.

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.820
We got one.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.750
But with all the stray cats in the neighborhood,

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:59.820
I told Mickey to put it outside.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:03.590
You're all the same. Give a plastic hand to a man.

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.160
Besides, I don't even know your name.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.160
Doctor what, huh?

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.720
He's neutralized. Do you want to see?

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:40.260
A dead arm.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.160
Are you sure?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:46.490
Hey, wait a minute, you can't run like that.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:48.390
Yes, I can. Look, it's all me.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:48.930
Goodbye.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.670
But the arm, it moved, it tried to kill me.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:52.750
I take it to study it.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:54.900
Don't go like that, it's not nice.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.810
Tell me what's going on.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:57.830
No, no.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:04.620
In this case, I'm going to see the police. I'm going to tell them everything.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:08.370
And you said that the people I'm going to talk to are likely to be killed.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:12.060
You choose. Tell me what's going on, or I'll tell you everything.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:13.680
It looks like blackmail, doesn't it?

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:14.780
In a way.

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:15.500
Well, it's wrong.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.860
Who are you?

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.260
I told you, the Doctor.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.090
Yes, but Doctor what?

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.130
Just the Doctor.

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:22.930
The Doctor.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:23.530
Hi!

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:27.480
You think you're impressing me?

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:28.660
In a way.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.300
Please, tell me, I've seen enough of it.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.450
Are you from the police?

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:39.900
No, I'm just a traveler, I'm far away from home.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.990
But what did I do wrong? Why is this plastic thing trying to kill me?

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:48.910
Oh, you think the whole world turned against you, but you are an accident, you were there, that's all.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.390
He tried to kill me!

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:51.890
He has after me, not after you.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.390
Last night in the store, I was there, you landed and you almost missed everything.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:58.630
This morning, I was looking for this arm and he was also looking for me.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:14:59.950
If he attacked you ...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.220
It's because you were on my way.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:05.470
So if I understand correctly, you say that the whole world would have after you, is that right?

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:06.510
In a way.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:07.630
Are you convinced?

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:08.770
In a way.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:13.350
But for this plastic story, who else is aware?

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:14.450
No one.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.440
What? Are you alone?

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.590
Who else is here?

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:21.740
Humans spend their time eating, sleeping and watching TV.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.120
During this time, there is war all around them.

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.560
Hey, start from the beginning.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:34.950
If we found ourselves in front of living plastic, I wouldn't like it, but we never know if it would happen.

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:36.550
How would you kill it?

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.980
The thing projected life into this arm.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.960
All I've done is send a signal.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.960
It's like a radio signal?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.260
A brain signal. Ziette?

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:49.540
Yes, but who controls this signal?

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:50.180
Long story.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.360
But what is it for, tell me?

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:55.160
Shop window models, I don't see why.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.650
Are they probably people who want to ruin business?

00:15:59.010 --> 00:15:59.410
No.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:01.300
I'm kidding.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.100
It's not the war of the prices.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:08.450
They want to infiltrate humans to destroy them.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.600
Do you believe me at least?

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:11.380
No.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:12.340
But you always listen.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.640
Be nice, Doctor.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.540
Tell me, who are you?

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:26.750
I'm going to teach you something about your planet.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.300
It's like when you're a kid.

00:16:32.076 --> 00:16:38.076
The first time you are told that the Earth is spinning on itself, you can't believe it, because everything around you looks immobile.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.440
I can feel it.

00:16:45.612 --> 00:16:46.772
The rotation of the Earth.

00:16:48.364 --> 00:16:51.484
On our feet, the ground moves at more than 1600 km per hour.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:57.500
The planet revolves around the sun at 108,000 km per hour, and I can feel it.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.500
We are crossing this space, you and me.

00:17:00.316 --> 00:17:03.876
Hanging on the skin of this tiny planet, what if we let it do it?

00:17:07.772 --> 00:17:08.452
Voilà, c'est moi.

00:17:09.276 --> 00:17:11.276
So you have to forget me, Rose Tyler.

00:17:13.084 --> 00:17:14.084
Hello at home!

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:20.010
You're a little woman, aren't you?

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.290
Yes, only in a clean cup.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.410
It doesn't mean to rinse, it means to wash.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:28.510
Can I use the computer?

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:29.780
Yes, it's an excuse.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.700
And you don't read my messages !

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.310
Plastic

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:14.840
Doctor Blue Box, where did you see this man? Contact me.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:19.090
But why did you come with me?

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:22.460
There's nothing to worry about, he has a wife and children.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.550
And who told you? It's him!

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:27.290
And that's exactly what a predator of the net would say, right?

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:55.740
Hello, I'm waiting for Clive. We've sent messages.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:59.300
Oh, Dad! It's another one of your crazy ones!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:02.800
Oh!

00:20:02.812 --> 00:20:07.012
Sorry. Hello. You must be Rose. I'm Clive, you know.

00:20:07.012 --> 00:20:09.812
I'm warning you, my little friend is in the car, he's waiting for me.

00:20:09.812 --> 00:20:11.412
In case you want to kill me.

00:20:11.412 --> 00:20:13.012
No, promise, no murders.

00:20:14.204 --> 00:20:15.204
Who's there?

00:20:15.388 --> 00:20:20.388
Oh, it's about the doctor, she came to my site, but I ask you to enter, enter.

00:20:22.268 --> 00:20:22.768
She?

00:20:23.996 --> 00:20:27.316
She visited your website that talked about the doctor, so it's...

00:20:27.356 --> 00:20:27.856
L !

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:37.780
Most of the files are sensitive, I couldn't send them to you, they can be intercepted, you understand.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:43.910
If you dig enough, if you keep your mind free, this doctor could appear anywhere.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:49.070
Political newspapers and conspiracy theories, even in ghost stories.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.910
No family name, no first name, the doctor.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.740
Only the doctor.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:59.970
This name of doctor, apparently transmitted from father to son, seems to be a herit...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.980
He's your doctor, isn't he?

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:03.010
Yes.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:06.510
I got this picture in the Washington Public Archives last year.

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.790
I got this picture on the Internet, but...

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:10.880
Look at the original.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:25.380
November 22, 1963.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:28.100
The assassination of President Kennedy.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:29.080
You see?

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:32.290
Maybe it's his father?

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.220
Let's take a look in the past.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.740
April 1912.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:41.340
Here's a picture of the Daniels, a family from Southampton.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:42.510
With a friend.

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:47.250
It was taken the day before they were supposed to travel on the Titanic.

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:50.910
But for some unknown reason, they canceled their trip and survived.

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:52.860
And I also have this.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.580
1883, another doctor.

00:21:58.040 --> 00:21:59.880
Look, what a resemblance.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:06.050
They are identical. This drawing was made on Sumatra's coast just before the Krakatoa woke up.

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.940
This doctor is a legend that travels in our history.

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:12.380
When a disaster is coming, he is there.

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:14.650
He sends the storm on his way.

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:16.610
He travels with his companion.

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:17.740
Who is that?

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:19.130
Death.

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:51.210
If you saw it, Rose, I can tell you one thing, our world is in danger.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:28.010
Is there someone?

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:28.510
Sorry

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:36.680
If you see him go home, you just have to pray.

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:01.710
I'm ready!

00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:24.120
